# Problem #6 — Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock

Given an array of stock prices, find the maximum profit possible by buying once and selling later.

The buy day must occur before the sell day.

## Approach

Track two values while scanning the array:

* **Minimum price** seen so far.
* **Maximum profit** achieved so far.

For each price, either update the minimum price or calculate the profit from selling at the current price and update the maximum profit.

This avoids nested loops and processes the array in a single pass.

**Time:** O(n)
**Space:** O(1)

## Key Learning

* Maintain the minimum value seen so far rather than finding the global minimum.
* Calculate the result incrementally while scanning.
* One-pass algorithms can eliminate unnecessary nested loops.

## SDET Relevance

This pattern is useful when scanning time-ordered test data or metrics where the best result depends on maintaining the minimum or maximum value observed so far.
